## 📶 **3. BLE GATT Characteristics**

The Devboard exposes multiple **GATT Services** — grouped by function.

| **Service**       | **Characteristic Name** | **UUID (example)** | **Properties** | **Function / Description**                                           |
| ----------------- | ----------------------- | ------------------ | -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `Battery Service` | `Battery Level`         | `0x2A19`           | Read / Notify  | Reports % battery                                                    |
| `Device Info`     | `Device ID`             | `0x2A23`           | Read           | Unique ID for board                                                  |
| `Health Data`     | `PPG Sensor Data`       | `C1B1-...`         | Notify         | Sends live heart rate/PPG data                                       |
|                   | `Temperature Data`      | `C1B2-...`         | Notify         | Sends temperature readings                                           |
|                   | `Sensor Status`         | `C1B3-...`         | Read           | Indicates sensor operational status                                  |
| `Control Service` | `Command`               | `C1C1-...`         | Write          | App sends control commands (start/stop/reset)                        |
| `Config Service`  | `Settings`              | `C1D1-...`         | Write/Read     | App writes configuration bytes                                       |
| `Error Service`   | `Error Code`            | `C1E1-...`         | Notify         | Sends current error code on fault                                    |
| `System`          | `State`                 | `C1F1-...`         | Read/Notify    | Indicates current system state (Idle, Measuring, Transmitting, etc.) |

➡️ Each characteristic has **read/write permissions** defined and must be subscribed for notifications in the app.

