## ⚙️ **4. Device Settings Byte Structure**

This allows configuration of sensors and system parameters via BLE writes.

| **Byte Offset** | **Parameter**        | **Value Range** | **Default** | **Description**                         |
| --------------- | -------------------- | --------------- | ----------- | --------------------------------------- |
| 0               | PPG Sampling Rate    | `0x00`–`0x03`   | `0x02`      | 0 = 10Hz, 1 = 25Hz, 2 = 50Hz, 3 = 100Hz |
| 1               | Temp Sampling Rate   | `0x00`–`0x02`   | `0x01`      | 0 = 1Hz, 1 = 2Hz, 2 = 5Hz               |
| 2               | LED Mode             | `0x00`–`0x03`   | `0x01`      | Controls LED intensity pattern          |
| 3               | BLE Adv. Interval    | `0x00`–`0x05`   | `0x02`      | Interval for advertisement packets      |
| 4               | Sleep Timeout        | `0x00`–`0x0A`   | `0x05`      | Time in minutes before auto-sleep       |
| 5               | Measurement Duration | `0x00`–`0x3C`   | `0x1E`      | Duration (seconds) for auto-stop        |
| 6               | Reserved             | —               | —           | Future sensor integration               |
| 7               | Checksum             | Calculated      | —           | Data integrity validation               |

➡️ These bytes are written to the **“Settings Characteristic”** under the Config Service.

