## 🔄 **5. State Table**

This sheet explains **device operational states** and transitions.

| **State**               | **Meaning**                   | **Triggered By**        | **Next State**   |
| ----------------------- | ----------------------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------- |
| **0x00 – Boot**         | Device startup initialization | Power On                | Idle             |
| **0x01 – Idle**         | Ready, BLE advertising        | Power connected         | Measure          |
| **0x02 – Measuring**    | PPG + Temp active             | Command `0x10`          | Transmitting     |
| **0x03 – Transmitting** | BLE notifications active      | After measurement ready | Idle             |
| **0x04 – Sleep**        | Low power mode                | 5 min inactivity        | Idle (on wake)   |
| **0x05 – Error**        | Fault state                   | Error detected          | Idle after reset |

➡️ Transitions follow the App Dev Guide commands and can be visualized as:

```
Boot → Idle → Measuring → Transmitting → Idle → Sleep
        ↘ (Error Detected) → Error → Idle
```

